{
  "name": "Rite Noir",
  "type": "dark",

  "_comment": [
    "Derived from ../../tokens.json. Editor background is #04060a; the sidebar,",
    "tabs and widgets step up through #0a0f16 / #10171f / #18212d. Those steps",
    "are ~1.05:1 apart on purpose — the separation is carried by #1c2634 borders,",
    "so the window reads as one dark surface with edges rather than as a set of",
    "grey boxes.",
    "",
    "Rite scopes come from editors/vscode/syntaxes/rite.tmLanguage.json and the",
    "colours from grammar/palette.json, so a .rite file matches the site and",
    "`rite render` output exactly. Semantic highlighting is left off: rite-lsp",
    "deliberately does not advertise semantic tokens (see IMPLEMENTATION.md), and",
    "turning it on here would let other languages' semantic colours override the",
    "TextMate rules below inconsistently."
  ],

  "semanticHighlighting": false,

